# Mobile app environment.
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and adjust for your environment:
#   cp apps/mobile/.env.example apps/mobile/.env
#
# Expo inlines any variable prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_* into the JS bundle at build
# time — the same deal as Vite's VITE_* on web. Nothing here is secret, and
# nothing secret may be added: assume every value below is readable by anyone
# who has the app. Cognito still requires user credentials to issue a token.
#
# Values mirror apps/web/.env with the prefix swapped (VITE_ -> EXPO_PUBLIC_),
# so mobile authenticates against the same user pool as web.
#
# NOTE: Metro bakes env values into the bundle. After editing, restart with
# `pnpm dev --clear` or the old values persist.

# --- AWS Cognito -------------------------------------------------------------
# Same pool as web, so the same users, MFA settings and groups apply.
EXPO_PUBLIC_COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=us-east-1_Pi5LBJ3ZG
EXPO_PUBLIC_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=4vupgqt07fuia6a9df1fob36g9
EXPO_PUBLIC_COGNITO_DOMAIN=dev-dispatch-auth.auth.us-east-1.amazoncognito.com

# Hosted-UI (OAuth) redirects. Web derives these from window.location.origin,
# which does not exist on native — a native app redirects back through its URL
# scheme instead (`scheme: "dispatch"` in app.json).
#
# Left commented until the hosted-UI flow is wired up: username/password sign-in
# via Amplify does not use them. Before uncommenting, the Cognito app client must
# have these exact callback/sign-out URLs registered, or the redirect fails with
# an "invalid redirect_uri" error from Cognito rather than from the app.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_COGNITO_REDIRECT_SIGN_IN=dispatch://
# EXPO_PUBLIC_COGNITO_REDIRECT_SIGN_OUT=dispatch://

# --- API ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by apps/mobile/src/api/setup.ts to point @dispatch/api at this origin.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://dev.api.dispatch.newleveltech.net/api/v1

# --- Environment -------------------------------------------------------------
EXPO_PUBLIC_ENV=development
